Subject: [PATCH 00/35] LG Fx0 runtime integration checkpoint (local draft)

Local integration checkpoint only. This mixed-subsystem series has not been
sent for review and is not a claim of upstream submission readiness.

Reconstruct the complete Fx0 runtime candidate from the pinned pre-DMP base,
retaining the DMP/display prerequisites and CPU/CPR integration. The original
39 source patches are preserved in the manifest. Four original prefixes fail
their own CPR clock bindings because the stricter requirement precedes the
matching qualification DTB. Group source patches 33-35 and 37-39 as atomic
integration transitions, yielding 35 commits with the exact same final tree.
Every exposed CPR qualification DTB now passes its own prefix binding.

The 35 mail patches replay cleanly with git am from the exact base, reproducing
the complete final tree and commit ID. Final source matches all 48 changed
files in the frozen host/Alpine builds. The final Alpine source package passes
its actual community configuration check, signed-APK metadata/binary checks,
embedded kernel trust-list comparison and all 464 module signatures. Modified
payload/signature/metadata and a different build certificate are rejected.
The existing final-source host suite passes 114 checks; the package exporter
passes seven checks. All 35 prefixes pass the 20 affected ARM object targets with W=1. These
object checks do not replace full intermediate kernel links or hardware tests.

Hardware scope remains narrower. One ordinary-DTB Fedora-Clang RAM image
boots four CPUs, binds the L2 master, records cpu-spc use and returns on its
timer to unchanged installed r50. Its 22 HTTP status/dmesg pairs and serial
log support that bootstrap result. The Alpine artifact remains unbooted. The separate CPR DTB now reaches
moduleless RAM diagnostics but its provider probe fails -EINVAL: CPU stays at
800 MHz and no CPUfreq policy appears. Its 181.623794-second return reaches
unchanged r50, with owner-confirmed display/touch. This does not qualify the
300 MHz/MX startup handoff. A second instrumented RAM image identifies
the reference-source check returning -EINVAL. A read-only native word at
APCS+0x64 is 1, the stock AHB selection; the stock driver explicitly selects
XO=0. Controlled reference setup while CPR is stopped and verified readback
remain to implement. Pstore confirms that diagnostic return at 181.601496
seconds, and the owner confirms display/touch on its newest unchanged r50 boot. Higher eligible rates, actual rails/feedback, thermal, suspend,
fail-stop recovery and the earlier r51 EDL cause remain unqualified. The
input-dependent lk2nd download defect has only an encoding workaround.

Before submission, split/rebase the changes onto current subsystem trees,
review original contributor attribution and DCO certification, and complete
the relevant physical and intermediate-build gates. Tentative recipients
come only from the pinned integration MAINTAINERS and must be refreshed.
No certification, review or test trailers have been invented. No firmware,
calibration, private identifiers or signing keys are included.

